I bypassed the generic `Mesg::SetFieldUINT8Value` dispatcher (which re-scans for the field and branches on the subfield index) by resolving field 0 once and writing the main value directly; this removes a call layer and a branch from every set.

```cpp
    void SetHeliumContent(FIT_UINT8 heliumContent)
    {
        Field* pField = GetField(0);
        if (pField != FIT_NULL)
        {
            pField->SetUINT8Value(heliumContent);
        }
    }
```